    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, and welcome. I'm Dr. [Name], a psychiatrist. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hi. Well, I guess what brings me in is this... constant restless feeling. It’s like I’m just wound too tight and I can’t fully settle down. Even when I’m supposed to be doing something calm, you know? Like sitting through a planning meeting at work—I’m a retail buyer, and our seasonal forecasting meetings are just endlessly long. Actually, last week, my manager brought in these scones from that new bakery on 4th street, the one with the green awning? They were so incredibly dry, I couldn't even finish half of one, and they didn't even bring butter. \n\nBut anyway, I just can't settle during those meetings. Or even when I'm trying to do something relaxing on my own time, like painting, or doing yoga. I started this new Vinyasa class on Tuesdays, and the instructor plays this really strange ambient flute music that just echoes off the studio walls and... wait, what was I saying? Right, the restlessness. I just always feel wound up, even when I'm supposed to be completely still.",
