    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you feel this wound-up, restless feeling, is your mind also racing with worries or concerns? Or is it more that your body just feels like it needs to move, even if your mind isn't particularly anxious?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I wouldn't say I'm worried about anything. It's not like an anxious thing where I'm stressing over, I don't know, paying bills or something. It's definitely more of a physical thing. Like my body just has all this pent-up energy and needs to do something, so my foot will just start tapping on its own. \n\nI mean, my thoughts do jump around a lot, but it's not worry. It's more like... I'll be sitting there and suddenly remember I need to call our vendor about the summer linen order. We're doing this huge push on breathable fabrics this year because last summer was just so incredibly hot. I remember my air conditioning went out in July and it took the repair guy three days to come out. Three days! And he charged an absolute fortune just to replace this tiny little fuse that I probably could have bought at the hardware store for two dollars if I'd known what to look for. The guy's name was Jerry, I think, and he kept tracking mud onto my hallway runner... \n\nBut, um, anyway. No, it's not anxiety or worrying. It's really just my body feeling like I need to get up and walk around or do something with my hands.",
