    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you been experiencing this restless, wound-up feeling with the racing thoughts and the need to move around? Has this been going on your whole life, or did it start more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, I guess I've always been a bit high-energy, but it really became noticeably harder to manage... let's see, it's been about two years and two months now. Right around the time when the conflicts with my in-laws started taking over, well, basically all of our evenings. \n\nMy mother-in-law, she just has this way of making these little comments, you know? Like she’ll come over and point out that the throw pillows on the couch don’t match the rug. And I’m like, 'Susan, they’re supposed to be complementary, not identical.' I spent three weeks sourcing those pillows from a boutique in Santa Fe. They have this gorgeous hand-woven geometric pattern—the artisan actually uses natural dyes made from local plants. It’s fascinating, really, the whole process of extracting the color from the roots and leaves. I watched this whole documentary about it on a Sunday afternoon when my husband was watching football. He always watches the games with the volume turned up way too loud. I keep telling him it's going to ruin his hearing, and then he'll be one of those older men who just nods and smiles at dinner parties because he can't hear a word anyone is saying... \n\nBut, right, the timeline. Yeah, it's been about two years and two months since it got really hard to just sit still and deal with it all.",
